{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792947821,"nonce":"Wj5kR5zCLWv4lSDdsLF1C4zULyU=","title":"A frame built for one function runs another's opcodes under caribou when a worker thread is created while a plugin's callbacks are in play","message":"**What happens**\n\nUnder `caribou run` (the Ash interpreter), ashui's CodeDiffComponent fixture panics in the interpreter's register file:\n\n    thread 'caribou-world-0' panicked at ash_interp/src/frame.rs:220:9:\n    cannot read register 26: the frame holds 5, and was built for function index 392. A frame sized for one function is running another's opcodes\n    ... execute_entrypoint::fiber_closure_runner \u003c- _hlp_call_method \u003c- _hlp_dyn_call\n    thread 'main' panicked at frame.rs:220:9:\n    cannot write register 1550: the frame holds 0, and was built for function index 580.\n\nThe worker thread (`Thread.create(() -\u003e while (true) jobs.pop(true)())`, ashui's `ashui.core.Worker`) dies in the fiber closure runner first; main then finds its own frame emptied. The same program with the same Ash and caribou, with blinc_abi loaded as an HDLL, passes (48 checks); with blinc_abi as a Caribou plugin (callbacks go through `host::call`) it panics. The fixture without its worker section passes (45 checks). A worker started at the top of `main` panics too, so creating the thread inside a callback is not the cause.\n\n**Reproducer**\n\nashui at 534a0be, blinc_abi at fc029ec, caribou with the staged Ash:\n\n    cd ashui/tests\n    sh run.sh render-caribou          # builds the plugin into bin/caribou/plugins\n    mkdir -p bin/cb/plugins \u0026\u0026 cp bin/caribou/plugins/* bin/cb/plugins/\n    haxe --class-path ../haxe --class-path ../../ash/haxelib/ash-simd -D ash_simd -lib hashlink -lib tink_hxx -lib caribou \\\n      -D ashui_caribou -w -WDeprecated --macro 'ashui.ui.Markup.enable()' --class-path ../components/haxe \\\n      --class-path fixtures/components -main CodeDiffComponent -hl bin/cb/code-diff-component.hl\n    (cd bin/cb \u0026\u0026 caribou run code-diff-component.hl)\n\nThe panic comes at `tree.flush()` after `original.set(big)` and `modified.set(bigEdited)` (30000 lines each): a Watch body starts `Worker.run(() -\u003e CodeDiffer.lines(a, b), ...)` and the worker runs while main goes on.\n\n**What was tried**\n\nSmall programs that run a busy worker beside a main thread calling plugin functions, with a 1700-register main frame, with a plugin callback that creates the thread, and with large text through the plugin all pass. Dropping `inline` from the Haxe shim functions moved the failing function index (580 to 581) and changed nothing else.\n\n**Next**\n\nFind what lets the fiber closure runner build a frame for the wrong function, and why main's frame reads as empty afterwards. Related: e961524 (a host's closure entry called without a trap).","files":null}]}